Ever wondered how your video call stays smooth while your file download takes its time?"
 Let’s talk about TCP vs UDP — two protocols that silently power your internet experience.

🔗 TCP (Transmission Control Protocol):

 ✅ Connection-oriented – sets up a reliable session
 ✅ Guarantees delivery and correct order of packets
 ⏳ A bit slower due to extra overhead (like handshakes)
 🧠 Used in: HTTP/HTTPS, email, file transfers

⚡ UDP (User Datagram Protocol):

 🚫 No connection – just sends and forgets
 ❌ Doesn’t guarantee delivery or order
 ⚡ Super fast with minimal overhead
 🎮 Used in: Video streaming, VoIP, online gaming
